{
  "schema": "perch-native-parity-fixture/1",
  "screen": "select",
  "note": "Floating screen: it is drawn through a portal into the page body and placed against the window, so the reference is the whole default 1280x800 window on the app's backdrop and every box is in window coordinates. Perch's one dropdown (stock-ui/select): a field (here a button) that keeps focus and a `role=listbox` drawn through a portal, fixed under the field (4 px gap, left aligned to it, as wide as its longest label and at least as wide as the field, at most 320 px high; it flips above the field when there is less than 160 px below and more above; it slides back inside the window when it would pass the right edge, 8 px margin). The harness holds the value as a caller does and places the field at `props.at` (window coordinates, width in px), with the SDK's default field class and `w-full`, so the field is as wide as `at.width`. Opening it is a click on the field (`steps`); the keyboard is key events on the field.",
  "dataFrom": "sidebar",
